Hey, thanks for checking out FieldGuide Agent!

This project was built with countless late nights, real sweat debugging WebSocket
timeouts, and a genuine passion for helping field technicians in remote areas.
If this code helps you in any way -- whether you learn from it, build on top of it,
or use it as a starting point for your own thing -- that's awesome, and exactly
why it's open source.

All I ask is simple: keep my name in the credits. Not because I'm chasing fame,
but because it's a small way of saying "someone poured their heart into this."
A mention in your README, a comment in your code, or even just a shoutout --
that's more than enough.

